-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",102,{
[3233]="70025381\n1\tFind Suvulch somewhere near Lhanuch\tYou last saw Suvulch at Wadu's favourite tree, on a rise by the ox-pens, west of Lhanuch. Nona is angry at her father Suvulch for his cruel treatment of Wadu while Wadu was still alive, and she wants you to tell Suvulch so.\n2\tDefeat hostile Dunlendings throughout Enedwaith\tHostile Dunlendings can be found throughout Enedwaith. Suvulch has challenged you to a competition to see who can defeat the most Dunlendings of enemy clans in honour of Wadu.\n3\tTalk to Suvulch\tSuvulch is by Wadu's favourite tree, on a rise by ox-pens west of Lhanuch, and hostile Dunlendings can be found throughout Enedwaith. Suvulch has challenged you to a competition to slay hostile Dunlendings in memory of Wadu.\n4\tFind Radanir at the grove of trees east of Lhanuch\tRadanir is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees to the east of the Uch-lûth village of Lhanuch. Suvulch told you that Radanir was looking for you about an urgent matter.\n5\tRead the letter on the crate by Radanir\tA second letter from Ergothorn is on the crate near Radanir, at the camp-site of the Grey Company in the grove of trees east of Lhanuch. Radanir has found a second letter from Ergothorn and wants you to read it and give your opinion on what the mysterious correspondent has to say.\n6\tTalk to Radanir at the grove of trees east of Lhanuch\tRadanir is at the camp-site of the Grey Company in the grove of trees east of Lhanuch. You have read Ergothorn's second letter, which calls for you to go to the defence of Zudrugund.\n",
[3234]="7002161E\n1\tFind Fúni Gem-cutter somewhere within Minas Elendúr\tFúni Gem-cutter is being held somewhere within the depths of Minas Elendúr, far to the east of Echad Eregion. You have learned the location of Fúni Gem-cutter and should now attempt his rescue.\n",
[3235]="70013AF8\n1\tDefeat goblins along the Silvertine Lodes (total: 18)\030Collect Crude Map (total: 4)\tGoblins can be found among the Silvertine Lodes, south and below the Great Delving, and their maps can be found within Gamil Filik, the mine they have occupied. Brogur asked you to slay goblins while you seek the Heart of Fire, and to keep an eye out for their maps; it is possible they discovered the forge and included it on their crude maps.\n2\tBring crude maps to Brogur\tBrogur is in the Chamber of Command, up the eastern stairs in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, located at the southern entrance to Durin's Way, north of the Great Delving. You have slain many goblins and collected their maps while searching for the Heart of Fire.\n3\tBring crude maps to Bósi\tBósi is in the Chamber of the Cross-roads, just outside the Chamber of Command. Brogur has not seen anything of use on the crude goblin-maps you found, but his cousin Bósi may have better fortune interpreting them.\n",
[3236]="70018F0F\n1\tTalk to Bróin\tBróin is resting on the Peaceful Path, located in the Mustering Hall, east of Sulnul-dûm and west of the Stone Hall, along Durin's Way. The entrance to the Peaceful Path is north-east of Buzun-ghâr. Bróin has sent word that he wishes to speak with you again. Orvar told you to treat Bróin kindly, believing that his trials in the watery den of the Watcher and losing his cousin to the forces of Mazog may have affected him deeply.\n2\tThe Chambers of Wisdom, Knowledge, and Deep Thought can be found throughout the Great Delving, as can Katûb-zahar. Any of these places may have the mining records Bróin was tasked with finding. Bróin is dissatisfied with the mindless tasks his father Brogur has assigned him, and he is extremely frustrated that the dwarves are doing such work as this while Bori remains prisoner to the forces of Mazog.\t\n3\tBring mining records to Bróin\tBróin is on the Peaceful Path, located in the Mustering Hall, east of Sulnul-dûm and west of the Stone Hall, along Durin's Way. The entrance to the Peaceful Path is north-east of Buzun-ghâr. You have recovered some of the mining records that Bróin's father wanted him to find, but they include some curious details in which Bróin will be most interested.\n",
[3237]="700143D8\n1\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership, off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek, with Brogur. Brogur has told you that his nephew Bori has devised a daring plan to strike a blow against the White Hand Orcs in Moria, and wants you to help him with his preparations.\t\n2\tTalk to Bori\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership, off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. You have helped Bori prepare for his daring strike on the White Hand, and should now report to him.\n",
[3238]="700143DA\n1\tFind guarded junction on Eastern Road\030Collect Barrel of Black Powder (total: 8)\tThe guarded junction on the Eastern Road is in Nud-melek, and the White Hand encampment of Stazgnâkh is located among the Redhorn Lodes. Bori has asked you to investigate the guarded junction along the Eastern Road, and to collect barrels of black powder from the White Hand encampment of Stazgnâkh so you will become familiar with it.\n2\tBring black powder barrels to Bori\tBori is in the Chamber of Leadership, off the Twenty-first Hall in Zelem-melek. You have assessed the strength of the force at the guarded junction along the Eastern Road and found two entrances into Stazgnâkh, the White Hand encampment among the Redhorn Lodes.\n",
[3239]="7005A722\n1\tDecorate Vérnozal with Zhélruka runners (quantity: see journal)\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should decorate Vérnozal with Zhélruka runners for Prince Ingór.\n2\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n3\tPlant crystals in crystal planters throughout Vérnozal (total: 12)\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. You should place the crystals that you mined in the crystal planters scattered throughout Vérnozal.\n4\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tVérnozal can be found in Máttugard, by the Steepset. Prince Ingór wishes to talk to you.\n",
[3240]="7001AC5A\n1\tTalk to Lenglammel to travel to Azanarukâr\tLenglammel is in Gwathrendath, the Elf-camp among the Foundations of Stone. Lenglammel is waiting to speak to you in order to bring you to Magor for an assault on Azanarukâr. NOTE: Inspiration will assist you if you choose to undertake this challenge. This instance can only be completed by a solo or two person group.\n2\tTalk to Lenglammel in Gwathrendath\tLenglammel is in Gwathrendath, the Elf-camp among the Foundations of Stone. You have destroyed the relic of Gorothúl and sent both Gwathnor and Grawulun formless into the depths, for a time. You should report now to Lenglammel.\n3\tTalk to Haldir at Talan Haldir\tHaldir is on Talan Haldir, just outside the border of the Golden Wood. Lenglammel has sent you to Haldir to relay a message of importance: the expedition of the Golden Host must happen as soon as it is possible.\n",
[3241]="7001C1F0\n1\tHide behind upright stones on the road to Minas Gîl (total: 3)\tUpright stones can be found along the sloping road to Minas Gîl, east of Ost Galadh. Enedhel has asked you to hide behind upright stones on the road to Minas Gîl in order to learn how closely the eastern way to Dol Guldur is being watched by the Orcs.\n2\tTalk to Enedhel at Ost Galadh\tEnedhel is within Ost Galadh, in Emyn Lûm. You have hidden behind the upright stones on the road to Minas Gîl, east of Ost Galadh, and should return now to Enedhel with what you have learned.\n",
[3242]="7001C1F1\n1\tAssess the Orc-presence at Krul Lugu\tKrul Lugu is the Orkish name for a pair of Orc-fortifications in the centre of Taur Morvith, south of the Verdant Shrine. Erymbes has asked you to investigate the Orc presence at Krul Lugu and to then find her friend Malendol.\n2\tFind Malendol in or around Krul Lugu\tMalendol may be somewhere in or around the Orc-fortifications of Krul Lugu, in Taur Morvith. You have assessed the Orc-presence at Krul Lugu and should now search for Malendol, who may be in trouble.\n3\tTalk to Erymbes at the Verdant Shrine\tErymbes is at the Verdant Shrine, north of the Orc-camps of Krul Lugu, in Taur Morvith. You have scouted the Orc-camps of Krul Lugu and defended Malendol and should return now to Erymbes with what you have learned.\n",
[3243]="7001C1F2\n1\tCollect venom samples from spiders in the Scuttledells (total: 6)\tSpiders can be found throughout the Scuttledells. Gladiel has asked you to gather venom from the spiders of the Scuttledells by using the cloth she gave you.\n2\tBring the cloth containing venom samples to Gladiel by the Shrine of the Ancient One\tGladiel is by the Shrine of the Ancient One, in the Scuttledells. You have collected a number of venom samples from the spiders of the Scuttledells and should return them to Gladiel so she can examine them.\n",
[3244]="7001A97D\n1\tThe Elves of the Hidden Guard can be found within the cellar of the Haunted Inn. Bróin has asked you to speak with the Elves of the Hidden Guard about what must be done next.\t\n2\tTalk to Cúcheron at the Haunted Inn\tCúcheron is outside the Haunted Inn, located among the Dourstocks. You have obtained the opinions of the Elves of the Hidden Guard concerning what route to take to Dol Guldur and have received three different proposals.\n3\tAid Enedhel in Ost Galadh, in Emyn Lûm\030Aid Erymbes in Taur Morvith\030Aid Gladiel in the Scuttledells\tThree scouts have been sent into the Scuttledells, Emyn Lûm, and Taur Morvith. Cúcheron has asked you to speak with the Elves he sent to investigate the areas along the proposed routes of the Hidden Guard. Gladiel is in the Scuttledells, west of the Shrine of the Ancient One, near the border of Gathbúrz. Erymbes is in Taur Morvith, by the Verdant Shrine, south of the Wild Ruin. Enedhel is in Ost Galadh.\n4\tTalk to Cúcheron at the Haunted Inn\tCúcheron is outside the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks. You have done as Cúcheron asked by gathering information on the possible routes toward Dol Guldur and should now return to him.\n5\tTalk to Issuriel in the Haunted Inn\tIssuriel is within the cellar of the Haunted Inn, located among the Dourstocks. Based on the information you have provided, Cúcheron has decided that Issuriel's proposed route to Dol Guldur has the greatest chance of success. He wants you to inform her that this is the way the Hidden Guard will take.\n",
[3245]="70047296\n1\tTalk to Bósi in the Hall under the Mountain\tBósi is in the Hall under the Mountain, grieving for the loss of his cousin and the failure of the Iron Garrison.\n2\tTalk to Bósi and go with him to see King Thorin\tBósi is in the Hall under the Mountain, grieving for the loss of his cousin and the failure of the Iron Garrison.\n3\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.\n4\tSearch far south of Lûghash, by the slope of Orodruin, for the missing dwarf heroes\tHis treachery revealed, you should return to Dor Amarth and search south of Lûghash, close to the slope of Orodruin, to find the dwarves slain by Dómor.\n5\tExamine the hasty gravesite\tYou have found what appears to be a hasty gravesite in Dor Amarth. Was this the location of Dómor's treachery?\n6\tTalk to Laurík at the gravesite\tYou have found the location where Dómor hid the bodies of the dwarves he betrayed and killed.\n7\tTalk to King Thorin III at his throne in the Hall under the Mountain\tThorin III, King under the Mountain, is at his throne in Erebor.\n",
[3246]="70047B61\n1\tTalk to Pippin\tYou should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion to hear what, exactly, they are thinking about with regard to Mordor.\n2\tTalk to Merry\tYou should talk to Merry in Bâr Thorenion to hear his thoughts on where the two remaining half-orcs might be.\n3\tSearch for the half-orcs\tPippin and Merry have asked you to go in search of the two half-orcs who fled the last encounter. Merry believes they will be found somewhere in Dor Amarth, on the path to Barad-dûr.\n4\tExamine the dead half-orc\tPippin and Merry have asked you to go in search of the two half-orcs who fled the last encounter. You have found one of them, come to a bitter end, on the path to Barad-dûr, and should examine the corpse.\n5\tPippin and Merry have asked you to go in search of the two half-orcs who fled the last encounter. You should follow the trail leading from the one half-orc, in hopes of finding the other.\t\n6\tTalk to the half-orc\tPippin and Merry have asked you to go in search of the two half-orcs who fled the last encounter. Tracks leading from the corpse of the first have led at last to the second, who lives still. You should talk to him and learn what you can.\n7\tReturn to Bâr Thorenion\tReturn to Merry and Pippin in Bâr Thorenion with news of what you learned from the dying half-orc.\n8\tTalk to Gandalf\tOn returning to Bâr Thorenion, Gandalf has appeared and beckoned you over to speak with him.\n9\tTalk to Merry\tYou should talk to Pippin and Merry in Bâr Thorenion, telling them at least some of the whole truth, as Gandalf counselled you.\n",
[3247]="700472B1\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir in King Elessar's throne room\tMithrandir has come to the throne room of King Elessar, atop Minas Tirith.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir in the throne room and stand guard\tMithrandir has come to the throne room of King Elessar, atop Minas Tirith.\n3\tTalk to Mithrandir in King Elessar's throne room\tMithrandir has come to the throne room of King Elessar, atop Minas Tirith.\n4\tTalk to King Elessar in his throne room\tKing Elessar is in his throne room atop Minas Tirith.\n",
[3248]="70068268\n1\tTalk to Corudan at the amphitheatre\tCorudan is at the amphitheatre outside the city.\n2\tTalk to Daxamat at the amphitheatre\tDaxamat is at the amphitheatre outside the city.\n3\tFind the Hungry Deep Tavern that overlooks the Sail-haven\tThe Hungry Deep Tavern is located up a set of stairs in the Upper Ward, from where it overlooks the Sail-haven.\n4\tPatrons of the Hungry Deep Tavern may have information of use to you.\t\n5\tFind the Whelk and Cockle Tavern to the west, in the Sail-haven\tThe Whelk and Cockle Tavern is located to the west of the Hungry Deep, in the Sail-haven.\n6\tTalk to patrons of the Whelk and Cockle Tavern ([see journal]/2)\tThe Whelk and Cockle Tavern is not as popular as the last one you visited, but patrons here may still know something.\n7\tWhat has caused this sudden stillness?\tThe folk here seem to be studiously avoiding your gaze.\n8\tTalk to Rothog the Storm outside the Whelk and Cockle Tavern\tRothog the Storm is at the Whelk and Cockle Tavern in the Sail-haven.\n",
[3249]="7004E59A\n1\tFind the home of Authi Gem-cutter in the Dwelling-halls\tThe home of Authi Gem-cutter and his family can be found in the south-western corner of the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.\n2\tTalk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead\tAuthi Gem-cutter is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.\n3\tTalk to Mother Amma in the Jewelstead\tMother Amma is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.\n4\tTalk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead\tAuthi Gem-cutter is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.\n5\tFind the entrance to the New-lodes of Narathâk east of the entryway within the Lonely Mountain\tThe entrance to the New-lodes of Narathâk is located east of the Dwelling-halls, beyond the passage that runs from the entryway to the Hall Under the Mountain.\n6\tTalk to Gráfar Splitstone in the New-lodes of Narathâk\tAuthi Gem-cutter's brother Gráfar is in the New-lodes of Narathâk.\n7\tDefeat vermin in the New-lodes (total: 8)\tThe New-lodes of Narathâk are crawling with cave-claws and other pests, and Authi's brother Gráfar asked you to help make the mine safe for the miners by thinning out some of the vermin.\n8\tPick up the crate of precious stones by Gráfar Splitstone\tAuthi's brother Gráfar Splitstone has asked you to carry a crate of precious stones back to Mother Amma in the Jewelstead. The Gem-cutter family home is located in the south-west corner of the Dwelling-halls.\n9\tPick up the finely-crafted necklace and deliver it to Erfith on the west side of the Dwelling-halls\tMother Amma has asked you to pick up the finely-crafted necklace and deliver it to Erfith, the customer who requested it. Erfith can be found on the west side of the Dwelling-halls of Erebor, on one of the lower levels.\n10\tTalk to Erfith on the west side of the Dwelling-halls\tErfith the Quarrelsome is on the west side of the Dwelling-halls of Erebor, east of the Jewelstead and down the stairs.\n11\tTalk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead\tAuthi Gem-cutter is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.\n",
[3250]="70059A04\n1\tTalk to Durin in Máttugard\tPrince Durin has returned with you to Máttugard.\n2\tFind Bósi at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws, north of Máttugard\tDurin ordered Bósi of the Iron Garrison to scout the further reaches of the Mountain-home, and has asked you to meet up with them at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws, north of Máttugard.\n3\tTalk to Bósi at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws\tBósi is at the entrance to the Pit of Stonejaws.\n4\tDefeat creatures in the Pit of Stonejaws (total: 8)\030Find Bori to the north-west in the Pit of Stonejaws\030Talk to Bori in the Pit of Stonejaws\tBósi's son Bori has gone to search the crypts in the Pit of Stonejaws, and could use your assistance to the north-west.\n5\tBori asked you to search more of the crypts along the westward path, which eventually turns north and slopes upward.\t\n6\tBori has agreed to meet you by the upper crypts, further north in the Pit of Stonejaws.\t\n",
[3251]="7004E634\n1\tFind Khîl outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain\tKhîl might be found outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain.\n2\tTalk to Khîl outside the Lonely Mountain\tKhîl the Tale-spinner is outside the entrance to Erebor, regaling onlookers with his stories.\n3\tDemonstrate to Khîl that you are ready to listen to his tales\tKhîl the Tale-spinner is outside the entrance to Erebor, regaling onlookers with his stories.\n4\tTalk to Khîl and hear his tale\tKhîl the Tale-spinner is outside the entrance to Erebor, regaling onlookers with his stories.\n5\tUse agree\030Use ahem\030Use angry\030Use confused\030Use grumble\030Use no\030Use yes\tKhîl the Tale-spinner is outside the entrance to Erebor, regaling onlookers with his stories.\n6\tTalk to Khîl and hear his tale\tKhîl the Tale-spinner is outside the entrance to Erebor, regaling onlookers with his stories.\n7\tUse agree\030Use yes\030Use ahem\030Use angry\030Valves and pipes? No one else has mentioned such a machine at the battle\030Use grumble\030Use no\tKhîl the Tale-spinner is outside the entrance to Erebor, regaling onlookers with his stories.\n8\tTalk to Khîl and hear his tale\tKhîl the Tale-spinner is outside the entrance to Erebor, regaling onlookers with his stories.\n9\tUse agree\030Use yes\030Use ahem\030Use angry\030Use confused\030Use grumble\030Use no\tKhîl the Tale-spinner is outside the entrance to Erebor, regaling onlookers with his stories.\n10\tTalk to Khîl and hear his tale\tKhîl the Tale-spinner is outside the entrance to Erebor, regaling onlookers with his stories.\n11\tTalk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead\tAuthi Gem-cutter is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.\n",
[3252]="7006826A\n1\tTalk to Hármelak in her manor\tHármelak is in the main hall of her manor.\n2\tFind the courtyard in Hármelak's manor\tHármelak asked you to wait for her in the courtyard of her manor.\n3\tWait for Hármelak in the courtyard of her manor\tHármelak asked you to wait for her in the courtyard of her manor.\n4\tTalk to Hármelak by the courtyard\tHármelak has arrived in the courtyard.\n5\tFind the garden of Hármelak's manor\tHármelak asked you to wait for her in the garden to the north of the courtyard.\n6\tWait for Hármelak in the garden to the north\tHármelak asked you to wait for her in the garden to the north.\n7\tTalk to Hármelak in the garden of her manor\tHármelak has arrived in the garden of her manor.\n8\tFind the office to the north in Hármelak's manor\tHármelak asked you to wait for her in the office to the north.\n9\tWait for Hármelak in the office to the north\tHármelak asked you to wait for her in the office to the north.\n10\tTalk to Hármelak in the office of her manor\tHármelak has arrived in her office.\n",
[3253]="70059A05\n1\tLook out over the Pit of Stonejaws\tBori has asked you to look out over the Pit of Stonejaws, which contains the crypts of the many dwarf-families that were laid to rest over the years.\n2\tTalk to Bori by the upper crypts in the Pit of Stonejaws\tBori is by the upper crypts in the Pit of Stonejaws.\n3\tClear rubble from the entrance to the south-west\tBori needs your help to clear the rubble and debris away from the entrance to the south-west.\n4\tClear rubble from the entrance to the south-west\tBori needs your help to clear the rubble and debris away from the entrance.\n5\tClear rubble from the entrance to the south-west\tBori needs your help to clear the rubble and debris away from the entrance.\n6\tExplore the room you have unearthed from the rubble\tTogether, you and Bori have cleared the rubble away from the room to the south-west, and can now gain entrance.\n7\tExamine the broken mosaic in Zul-mazal\tA broken mosaic decorates one wall of this chamber.\n8\tTalk to Bori in Zul-mazal\tBori is in Zul-mazal.\n9\tFind Bósi outside Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws\tBósi is outside the fortress of Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws.\n10\tTalk to Bósi outside Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws\tBósi is outside Shakhajât in the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws.\n",
[3254]="70068269\n1\tTalk to Rothog the Storm outside Hármelak's manor\tRothog the Storm has escorted you from Hármelak's manor. He clearly believes his task is finished.\n2\tFind Azagath's water-carriers on a dock near the Harbour Warden's tower\tHármelak told you that every day Azagath's servants can be found on the docks by the Harbour Warden's tower, filling bowls with water to carry to the Citadel of Winds.\n3\tTalk to water-bearer Enât on the dock\tAzagath's water-bearers are on a dock by the Harbour Warden's tower.\n4\tTalk to water-bearer Ushu on the dock\tAzagath's water-bearers are on a dock by the Harbour Warden's tower.\n5\tPick up the bowl of water on the dock\tThe water-bearers will only allow you to accompany them into the Citadel if you can prove up to their task.\n6\tTalk to Ushu on the dock beside the Harbour Warden's tower\tAzagath's water-bearers are on the dock beside the Harbour Warden's tower.\n",
[3255]="7004E637\n1\tTalk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead and go with him to petition the king\tAuthi Gem-cutter is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.\n2\tTalk to Authi Gem-cutter in the Jewelstead\tAuthi Gem-cutter is in the Jewelstead, the Gem-cutter family home in the Dwelling-halls of Erebor.\n",
[3256]="70059A07\n1\tTalk to Imák outside Shakhajât\030Talk to Bróin outside Shakhajât\tBósi has asked Imák and Bróin to draw the defenders of Shakhajât out into the open.\n2\tTalk to Bósi outside Shakhajât\tBósi is outside Shakhajât. Given Bróin's discomfort with the plan, perhaps you should volunteer in his stead?\n3\tBósi has agreed that you can carry out Bróin's part of the plan: climbing either the left or right slope around the fortress and using a discarded horn of battle to draw forth some of the hobgoblins from Shakhajât.\t\n4\tMeet up with Bróin inside Shakhajât\tNow that you have carried out your part of the plan, you should join the dwarves inside Shakhajât.\n5\tTalk to Bróin inside Shakhajât\tBróin is inside Shakhajât and desires to speak with you.\n6\tTalk to the dwarf-woman Bróin saw within Shakhajât\030Defeat hobgoblins in the Pit of Stonejaws (total: 8)\tBróin has seen a dwarf-woman fighting in the fortress and wants you to check on her while you combat the forces inside Shakhajât.\n7\tTalk to Fastrith outside Shakhajât\tThe dwarves have made their presence known to Bósi's satisfaction and are now ready to meet up outside Shakhajât.\n8\tTalk to Bori outside Shakhajât\tBori is waiting to meet up with you outside Shakhajât.\n",
[3257]="70059A08\n1\tTalk to Fastrith outside Shakhajât\tFastrith Hawkfeast is outside Shakhajât.\n2\tTalk to Fastrith and travel with her to Zul-mazal\tFastrith is outside Shakhajât, waiting for you and Bori to bring her to Zul-mazal to examine the interesting mosaic.\n3\tTalk to Imák in Zul-mazal\tImák is standing in Zul-mazal, waiting to speak with you.\n",
[3258]="70068272\n1\tTalk to water-bearer Ushu on the dock beside the Harbour Warden's tower and accompany her to the Citadel of Winds\tWater-bearer Ushu is on the dock beside the Harbour Warden's tower, waiting to accompany you to the Citadel of Winds.\n2\tTalk to Thorongil by the Harbour Warden's tower\tYou have rescued Thorongil from the Kindred of the Coins... with a little help.\n3\tWait for the others to arrive\tYou have rescued Thorongil from the Kindred of the Coins... with a little help.\n4\tTalk to Nauriel by the Harbour Warden's tower\tNauriel is relieved to see that you have rescued her son from the Kindred of the Coins.\n",
[3259]="7004E638\n1\tGandalf is in the Wizard-home, east of the Jewelstead and up several stairs\tGandalf is in the room that was given to him in the Dwelling-halls, east of the Jewelstead and up several sets of stairs.\n2\tMeet up with Authi and Khîl outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain\tAuthi planned to meet you outside the entrance to the Lonely Mountain after you prepared for the journey and said good-bye to Gandalf.\n3\tTalk to Khîl outside the Lonely Mountain\tKhîl Tale-spinner is at the entrance to the Lonely Mountain.\n4\tTalk to Authi outside the Lonely Mountain\tAuthi Gem-cutter is at the entrance to the Lonely Mountain.\n5\tVisit Méthur, a friend of the Gem-cutters who lives in Hammerstead\030Find an entrance to the town of Utterby\030Defeat insects throughout the Ironfold (total: 10)\030Defeat beasts throughout the Ironfold (total: 12)\030Defeat Easterlings throughout the Ironfold (total: 14)\030Visit Arin, a friend of the Gem-cutters who lives in Járnfast but is likely fishing in the Redwater\030Look from the cliff's edge at Skald's Drop to survey the lands below\tAuthi has suggested you help the people of the Ironfold as you travel to Járnfast. Complete any four of the objectives Authi has suggested as you travel through the Ironfold to Járnfast.\n6\tTravel to the entrance of Járnfast, in the Ironfold\tThe entrance to Járnfast is in the north-east corner of the Ironfold.\n7\tTalk to Khîl at the entrance to Járnfast\tYou have successfully escorted Khîl to Járnfast and should now speak to him.\n8\tTalk to Authi at the entrance to Járnfast\tAuthi is at the entrance to Járnfast.\n",
[3260]="7004E639\n1\tFind Náin the Slakeless, Lord of the Ironfort, at his throne\tNáin the Slakeless, Lord of the Ironfort, can be found at his throne atop the northern ramps.\n2\tTalk to Náin the Slakeless in Járnfast\tNáin the Slakeless, Lord of the Ironfort, can be found at his throne atop the northern ramps.\n3\tFind Durin in the Quenching Trough opposite the entrance to Járnfast\tThe Quenching Trough is a low-ceilinged tavern opposite the entrance to Járnfast.\n4\tTalk to Durin in the Quenching Trough\tDurin is in the Quenching Trough, a low-ceiling tavern opposite the entrance to Járnfast.\n5\tTalk to Durin (again) in the Quenching Trough\tDurin is in the Quenching Trough, a low-ceilinged tavern opposite the entrance to Járnfast.\n6\tTalk to Náin the Slakeless in Járnfast\tNáin the Slakeless, Lord of the Ironfort, can be found at his throne atop the northern ramps.\n",
[3261]="70068271\n1\tTalk to Jajax by the Harbour Warden's tower\tJajax is by the Harbour Warden's tower.\n2\tTalk to Nimrodel by the Harbour Warden's tower\tNimrodel is by the Harbour Warden's tower.\n3\tThe successful completion of your mission to Umbar is the result of those who helped you, and many of them are now by the Harbour Warden's tower and want to speak with you.\t\n4\tTalk to Caebar by the Harbour Warden's tower\tCaebar is by the Harbour Warden's tower, a long way from his home.\n",
[3262]="70059A0A\n1\tTalk to Fastrith in Zul-mazal\030Talk to Bróin in Zul-mazal\tImák has asked if Fastrith and Bróin wish to investigate the dealings of the Angmarim cultists in Câr Bronach.\n2\tMeet up with Imák at the Witch-gate between the Pit of Stonejaws and Câr Bronach\tImák has suggested that you meet up at the Witch-gate, which can be found at the connexion between the Pit of Stonejaws and Câr Bronach.\n3\tTalk to Imák at the Witch-gate\tImák stands at the Witch-gate between the Pit of Stonejaws and Câr Bronach.\n",
[3263]="7004E63C\n1\tTalk to Durin in Járnfast\tDurin is at his uncle's throne in Járnfast.\n2\tMeet up with Durin east of Utterby, in the Ironfold\tDurin is east of Utterby, in the Ironfold.\n3\tTalk to Durin east of Utterby\tDurin is east of Utterby, in the Ironfold.\n4\tBiraisbij tharâkh: Jangovar tents on the eastern side of Utterby\030Biraisbij tharâkh: Jangovar tents on the southern side of Utterby\030Bini'zig utrâd (total: 4)\tDurin suggested using dwarf-phrases that will be unfamiliar to the Jangovar in order to confuse your foes and to attain strategic advantage when you move against them: Biraisbêj tharâkh, \"scouting the approaches.\" Bini'zêg utrâd, \"blinding the watchers.\" Mahinsês mamahkhafdân, \"rescuing the prisoners.\" Isgêr narakakâ, \"defeating the reinforcements.\" Ensêkh, \"setting a trap.\"\n5\tInteract with Prisoner of the Jangovar\tDurin suggested using dwarf-phrases that will be unfamiliar to the Jangovar in order to confuse your foes and to attain strategic advantage when you move against them: Biraisbêj tharâkh, \"scouting the approaches.\" Bini'zêg utrâd, \"blinding the watchers.\" Mahinsês mamahkhafdân, \"rescuing the prisoners.\" Isgêr narakakâ, \"defeating the reinforcements.\" Ensêkh, \"setting a trap.\"\n6\tIsgir narakakâ (total: 4)\030Ensikh to waylay the Jangovar at the cliff-face near Skald's Drop (total: 2)\tDurin suggested using dwarf-phrases that will be unfamiliar to the Jangovar in order to confuse your foes and to attain strategic advantage when you move against them: Biraisbêj tharâkh, \"scouting the approaches.\" Bini'zêg utrâd, \"blinding the watchers.\" Mahinsês mamahkhafdân, \"rescuing the prisoners.\" Isgêr narakakâ, \"defeating the reinforcements.\" Ensêkh, \"setting a trap.\"\n7\tTalk to Durin at Skald's Drop\tDurin is beneath the rising cliff-face at Skald's Drop.\n8\tTalk to Náin the Slakeless in Járnfast\tNáin the Slakeless, Lord of the Ironfort, can be found at his throne atop the ramps.\n9\tTalk to Durin in Járnfast\tDurin can be found by his uncle's throne in Járnfast.\n",
[3264]="70059A11\n1\tScout the Iron Pass in the north-western reaches of Câr Bronach\030Talk to Imák at the Iron Pass\030Defeat beasts in Câr Bronach (total: 4)\tThe Iron Pass is located in the north-western reaches of Câr Bronach, and Imák wants you to make the road there as safe as you can while investigating the enemy presence on that route to Angmar.\n2\tScout the Narrow Way between Câr Bronach and Elderslade\030Defeat beasts in Câr Bronach (total: 4)\tHaving scouted the Iron Pass, Imák thinks you should now do the same for the Narrow Way, the southern pass into Elderslade. He also wants you to continue your efforts to make the mountain paths safe for the Gabil'akkâ.\n3\tTalk to Imák at the Narrow Way\tYou have met up with Imák at the Narrow Way only to discover that a former companion also shows an interest in the situation at Câr Bronach.\n4\tTalk to Venko at the Narrow Way\tYour former companion Venko has also come to investigate the Narrow Way between Câr Bronach and Elderslade.\n5\tRead the crumpled parchment given to you by Venko\tVenko gave you a crumpled piece of parchment that he wrestled from one of the Angmarim, and is waiting for you to read it.\n6\tGive the crumpled parchment to Imák at the Narrow Way\tVenko has asked you to show the crumpled parchment to Imák.\n7\tTalk to Venko at the Narrow Way\tVenko is waiting to hear your thoughts at the Narrow Way between Câr Bronach and Elderslade.\n",
})
